## Stale row fix after review

Row 1 of `login-join-page.test.tsx` checked `toContain("<locale>:")`. That text reached the HTML
only through the draft marker, which renders the mocked translation `th:joinDraftMarker`. With the
approved status the marker is gone, so the row contradicted the spec. Test commit `a5aaac66b`
changes the row to two checks: the HTML holds the heading of `JOIN_COPY` for that locale, and the
HTML holds no `joinDraftMarker` key. The row keeps one reason comment (pin-bound row F7).

The row fails at the base for the right reason. At the base (`d726bc42a`, before Green's edit) the
th render held `<p data-draft="true" class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500 p-3">th:joinDraftMarker</p>`,
as the run at that commit shows. So `.not.toContain("joinDraftMarker")` fails there, and the heading
check passes. The bad check ran in a stash: a stash would move Green's uncommitted work, and the
order forbids it. The base render is the evidence.

